# Commits whose changes are pure formatting, listed so `git blame` can skip them.
#
# Usage:
#   git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# GitHub honours this file automatically when it is named exactly this and lives
# at the repository root.
#
# Add a commit here when it changes no behaviour -- a `cargo fmt` sweep, a
# line-ending normalisation, a mass rename. Do NOT add ordinary commits: the
# point is that every entry can be ignored without losing information.
#
# NOTE: entries must be full 40-character SHAs. A short SHA silently does nothing.
#
# Empty for now. The initial commit is not listed because there is nothing before
# it to attribute work away from.
